    "Scouting Notes": "Converted shortstop who is relatively new to pitching and thus has a lot of untapped potential.\n Good athlete with a clean and smooth delivery and arm action, very repeatable.\n Fastball sits 90 92 mph with armside run and sink. Should continue to add velo as he gets older and as he focuses on pitching full time.\n Slider with 10 to 4 break shows above average potential. \n He also shows feel for a changeup that has fringe average potential. \n He fills up the strike zone, and shows good command on all his pitches, could be plus command at peak.\n Interesting player given he's only been a pitcher for a short period. Will be fun to see what he can add to his tool chest and what kind of velo he can pack on.\n Has the repertoire to stick as a starter and should have a lively arm that isn't as beat up as many college pitchers.",
